== Pipeline and first difference

Both routes use the exact matched model, request, mode, options, graph incidence,
particle/rule assignments, routing, weights and local formal factors. Source
admission and finalization differ: historical syntax infers and sorts decoded
port spellings; current retained templates keep actual owner indices and use
canonical named storage order. Finalization transports those identities and the
logical layout. Public export is the first observed differing interface
boundary: four QED declarations or 32 QCD declarations per mode, in addition to
the already justified whole-symbol presentation map. The nine other Row fields
agree. Shared atom algebra and momentum/Dirac evaluation cannot explain this
fully accounted shallow difference.

`FeynmanDiagram.serde_view` calls `NumeratorInterface.export`; `from_json`
uses `from_serde`, `admit`, reversible cooking, native slot parsing, and
`SymbolicTensor.from_declared_parts`. A declaration chooses logical axes; it
is not redundant syntax. Historical inference is not silently replaced by a
current declaration. The helper imports both the actual current payload and the
exact mapped historical payload with its interfaces still absent. The census
intentionally strips id/name; its public-import envelope restores them from the
captured name and exact typed hexadecimal u128 ID, without a floating conversion.

== Finite value and order proof

For each exact owner write historical logical slots as H and current slots as C.
The checked convention is H[i] = C[p[i]]. QED uses p = (1,0,2), QCD edges
p = (3,2,0,1), QCD vertices p = (5,4,0,1,2,3). Thus for an arbitrary old
component tuple a the corresponding current tuple b satisfies b[p[i]] = a[i].
Every slot includes the full representation definition, dimension, duality,
half-edge owner and lane. `geometry-proof.json` checks it against the actual
serialized half-edge order, endpoint, particle, vertex incidence and rule-slot
geometry. This is an incidence audit, not Python tensor inference.

Under this assignment every occurrence of every named field in the unchanged,
factorized local expression receives the same component. Leaf argument order,
scalar coefficients, internal scoped contractions and tensor-head definitions
are identical under the approved exact token map. Structural evaluation of that
same finite expression therefore gives the same value, for every component tuple
and arbitrary formal scalar data. No product is distributed, no Dirac trace is
performed, and no momentum, mass or parameter is assigned a numerical value.
This argument is stronger than a component spot check and distinct from Atom
identity alone: it supplies the actual typed field assignment and its ordered
layout correspondence. It is limited to the enumerated captured expressions.

The source-defined named `permuted(p)` changes only layout, retaining leaf
arguments and history. All 80 native transports satisfy
`current.permuted(p).same_value(historical)`; all 80 untransported comparisons
are false. No false comparison is hidden. The two canonical-to-logical maps
commute with p's inverse for every owner, and native component-network lowering
retains the declared boundary and the layout for all 80 owners on both routes.
This lowering uses the existing DummyLibrary and ParamTensor owners; it does not
execute or numerically evaluate components.

The type conventions are source-bound, not inferred from tag tolerance. The
Bispinor, color-fundamental and adjoint declaration blocks and their deriving
macro are byte-identical across historical/current sources. The relevant
Minkowski, LibraryRep dual/match/base methods and identity/metric factories also
match exactly. The Minkowski signature remains (1,-1,-1,-1); cofundamental dual
orientation remains explicit. `representation-source-proof.json` retains these
exact source blocks. `is_metric` and `is_composite` are derived by the owning
constructor from the admitted expression and match all captured owners. They
are not independently authorable serialized flags. Exact definition tables
remain load-bearing because native tag-subset tolerance proves no such identity.

== Actual consumers

`product_plan` uses named typed fields before considering positional/open or
matrix-channel inference. `compatible_pairs` maps canonical typed matches back
to logical positions. A historical pair (i,j) transports to (p_left[i],
p_right[j]); `alignment_indices` must receive those transported positions.
Named products retain canonical free-field order, preserving payload factors.
The packet checks 744 actual owner-pair plans by full typed physical identities,
and records each plan's raw positions. It checks every output layout across 244
stages of the actual `GraphExpressions.try_fold_numerator` selection and
`multiply` fold, then the public `FeynmanDiagram.numerator_of` result. All 28
graphs also exercise the actual `fragment_numerator` path via
`with_numerator_fragments`, which owns `multiply_many` and its typed canonical
key/history merge. Both routes agree at these consumers.

The unchanged geometry controls which vertices, paired propagators and boundary
crowns enter any fixed selection. The finite transport proof applies to those
same named factors; the explicit executed selection is the full graph with empty
exclusion. It is not a claim that all subsets were exhaustively executed. The
projector, prefactor and all other unaffected owners are admitted and checked
separately. Their equality and the established named-product rule preserve their
subsequent typed combination. No new grouped/sampled evaluator claim is made.

A cached positional plan is not interchangeable. There are 144 explicit witnesses
where interpreting a historical plan on current slots changes physical wiring.
The other 600 owner-pair plans happen to preserve wiring (including scalar/outer
plans); these are honest accepted holdouts. Recompute named plans or transport
each positional operand by its own proved permutation. No production patch is
recommended for the observed data: these owners and consumers pass.

== Controls, provenance and retained limits

All 80 affected owners reject duplicate, omitted, wrong-index and wrong-dimension
declarations at actual typed admission. Eight additional predeclared public
importer controls reject actual neighboring-owner slots in every cell and flipped
QCD cofundamental dual types in both modes. Twelve actual owner-binding controls
reject altered metric/composite claims. Their errors identify semantic admission
or owner-binding predicates; setup/parse failures receive no rejection credit.
Wrong-permutation checks fail as intended. QED's inverse is the same permutation,
so its 16 accepted inverse checks are not credited as negative controls.

